      "writtenOn": "2019-09-18T22:58:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ah.  it would still be more logical, reasonable, easier to read, etc. for the __nocfi function to be tiny.",
      "parentUuid": "a313a5f9_9085e034",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 549,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 549,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "199d7fa6623c8d6a3a7ee78a4def942b7ba0b818",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ecedf817_1812df93",
        "filename": "include/linux/filter.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 549,
      "author": {
        "id": 1058768
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-18T23:06:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The __nocfi function needs to be the one with the checking, because otherwise it provides a convenient gadget for jumping to arbitrary code.",
      "parentUuid": "b3ab2efb_e7b293b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 549,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 549,
        "endChar": 48
      },
